+The built-in choice for any supported interface can be replaced with a project-specific implementation.
+By default, MapStruct reads `mapstruct.properties` from the root of the mapping compilation classpath.
+A different classpath resource can be selected with the `mapstruct.configurationFile` annotation processor option.
+The selected resource uses standard Java properties syntax, for example:
+
+[source,properties]
+----
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.CustomList
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.CustomMap
+----
+
+The implementation must be a publicly accessible concrete class assignable to the configured interface.
+It must preserve the interface's unbounded type parameters and provide a public no-argument constructor without
+checked exceptions. If it also provides a usable public `int` constructor, MapStruct passes the source size as the
+initial capacity when available. Object factories continue to take precedence over configured implementations.
